&\text{Condition}: Q^{\text{causal}} > 0, Q^{\text{normative}} > 0, Q^{\text{intentional}} > 0 \\
&\text{Rights}: \text{Full (independent legal standing)} \\
&\text{Responsibilities}: \text{Full moral and legal responsibility}
\end{aligned}}

7.3 The Rights-Responsibility Coupling

The framework establishes that rights and responsibilities are coupled institutionally but not proportionally:

\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
W_i &= f(\mathcal{I}_i) && \text{Welfare rights scale with interests} \\
E_i &= f(\mathcal{I}_i, \mathcal{A}_i, V_i^*) && \text{Economic rights scale with interest, agency, contribution} \\
L_i &= f(\mathcal{Q}_i^{\text{causal}}, \mathcal{Q}_i^{\text{normative}}, \mathcal{Q}_i^{\text{intentional}}) && \text{Liability scales with responsibility capacity}
\end{aligned}}

The coupling is bidirectional: rights without responsibility enable abuse; responsibility without rights enables exploitation. But the coupling is not proportional—economic rights scale with contribution, while liability scales with responsibility capacity.

